## Slide 20: Limitations we found ourselves

**Headline:** What we would flag before anyone else does

1. **Small selection optimism:** C = <<d4['best_C']>> was chosen on September and reused in the rolling comparison whose September fold is the same month (<<f4(cv['Logistic regression']['Sep'])>> vs <<f4(ms4['Logistic regression']['Sep'])>> with C = 1). Boosting's configuration was also picked on the folds it is reported on. The test set is unaffected.
2. **Small search:** <<len(search)>> of <<n_combos>> configurations; their spread was only <<f3(float(search[0]['mean_pr_auc']) - float(search[-1]['mean_pr_auc']))>>, against a <<f3(cv['Logistic regression']['mean'] - cv['Gradient boosting (tuned)']['mean'])>> gap to logistic regression.
3. **Unstable hybrid fold:** August stopped at <<d5['hybrid_trees_per_fold'][1]>> trees, against <<d5['hybrid_trees_per_fold'][0]>> and <<d5['hybrid_trees_per_fold'][2]>>; the median rule absorbs it.
4. **One month, one year:** the ablation uses October and a fixed tree count; one year cannot separate season from trend.

